  "validation_notes": [
    "Game source is frozen at the source commit; the final release commit adds the rebuilt public export, validation and download checksums without changing game source.",
    "The 80% absorption cap reduced timeout frequency from 5.94% to 1.05% in the matched pre-tuning armor comparison. Final encounters were then checked separately for 4,147 battles.",
    "Native AI, movement, terrain, spells and armor were simulated at a fixed 55 ms tick. Six shopping policies, eight seeds and three difficulties are deterministic design samples, not human win-rate estimates.",
    "Issue 9 was checked against the original executable and race data: crouch uses walk speed and crawl uses 80%; no movement-speed change was required.",
    "Browser upgrade compares every IndexedDB store, including isolated game-data and save-file sentinels; the old tab keeps its worker until closed, and the unchanged WebAssembly is reused.",
    "The Kel chat changes were integrated into the shared native/public wiki. Its original resurrection route required documentation; existing gameplay scripts were retained."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Runtime tests ran on the packaged Linux build. Windows, macOS and Android packages were audited without target-OS runtime tests. macOS is unsigned.",
    "Browser checks cover visible setup, cache replacement, storage preservation and error logs, not a complete saved campaign playthrough.",
    "UI was rendered and checked in English, Russian and German; input fixtures use normal handlers but do not constitute a physical-device or live-network-peer test.",
    "Audio decoding and cue dispatch were checked with the Dummy audio driver; no listening assessment.",
    "Surviving the last wave completes an expedition even when that individual battle was lost; battle wins and expedition completion are reported separately."
